+# Tasks
+
+Reference: specs define the observable behavior (`openspec/changes/bench-feature/specs/task-handoff-mcp/spec.md`); design.md defines how (relax the params allowlist, type-check `_meta`, sync the twin by verbatim copy). Verification is intentionally scoped to this change's reachable surface: the plugin's own unittest file plus a byte-wise twin comparison — not the Rust workspace build or full suite.
+
+## 1. Accept `_meta` in the stdio tools/call params check
+
+- [x] 1.1 In `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py`, in the `tools/call` branch of `_mcp_stdio()`: accept `params` carrying an object-typed `_meta` (extend the accepted-field set to `{"name", "arguments", "_meta"}` and raise the existing pre-dispatch `ValueError` when `_meta` is present but not a JSON object); keep the dispatch call to `_mcp_tool_call(params.get("name"), params.get("arguments"), host, session)` unchanged so `_meta` never reaches dispatch, identity, or recorded signals. Verify: with a stdio pipe through `python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py --mcp-stdio` (env: `GRAPHHELM_EXECUTION_ID`, `GRAPHHELM_TOKEN_FILE`, `GRAPHHELM_RUNTIME_URL`, `GRAPHHELM_MCP_HOST`, `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID`), a `tools/call` with `params._meta = {"progressToken": "abc"}` returns a normal tool result while one with non-object `_meta` returns JSON-RPC `-32602`.
+- [x] 1.2 Add the stdio contract test required by the spec to `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py`, modeled on the existing MCP subprocess tests: one stdin stream containing an accepted `tools/call` with object `_meta` (assert non-error tool result), a `tools/call` with non-object `_meta` (assert `-32602`), and a `tools/call` with another top-level unknown field such as `progressToken` (assert `-32602`), asserting the Runtime stub received no requests beyond those of the single successful call, so refusals are proven pre-dispatch; leave the existing identity-override (`test_mcp_rejects_identity_override_and_oversized_request_before_runtime_io`) and oversized-frame tests untouched as regression guards. Verify: `python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py` runs the whole file green, new test included.
+
+## 2. Keep the Codex companion copy byte-identical
+
+- [x] 2.1 Copy the edited `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py` verbatim over `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py`. Verify: the two files compare identical byte-for-byte (e.g. `fc /b` reports no differences, or SHA256 of both files is equal).
+
+## 3. Integration check
+
+- [x] 3.1 Re-run `python plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py` (full file, confirming the closed-tools listing, identity-override refusal, and oversized-frame refusal still pass alongside the new `_meta` coverage) and re-run the byte-wise comparison of the two `task_handoff.py` copies from task 2.1. Verify: exit code 0 with zero failures/errors, and an identical-bytes report.
